{{Quote|I grow tired of asking this so it will be the last time: ''Where'' is the rebel base?|audio=WhereIsTheBase-ANH.flac|Grand Moff Tarkin to Princess Leia Organa|<ref name="Episode IV" />}}
The '''Great Temple''', also known as the '''Massassi outpost''', '''Base One''', or the '''Yavin 4 Rebel Base''' was a temple on the [[moon]] [[Yavin 4]] that served as the headquarters of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] early in the [[Galactic Civil War]]. In its struggle against the [[Galactic Empire]], the Rebel Alliance had refitted the ancient-looking [[stone]] structure that notably contained a [[Grand Temple's throne room|grand ceremonial chamber]], a control room, and a vast [[hangar]] for [[starfighter]]s. Following the [[Battle of Yavin]], the Alliance [[Evacuation of Yavin 4|evacuated]] the Great Temple and within [[3 ABY|three]] [[Standard year|years]], built and populated a new [[Echo Base|base of operations]] on the [[Water|snow]] planet [[Hoth]].

==History==
{{Quote|These temples were built by the Massassi race thousands of years ago, and they're still standing. Hard to believe.|Leia Organa, to Luke Skywalker|<ref name="A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy">''[[A New Hope: The Princess, the Scoundrel, and the Farm Boy]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Great_Temple_TRF.png|thumb|left|250px|Cutaway of the Great Temple]]
The Great Temple was constructed over 5,000 [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]]<ref name="BTM" /> by a group of [[Massassi]], a [[Slavery|slave]] [[Species|race]] once ruled by the [[Sith]], under the leadership of the [[Sith Lord]] [[Naga Sadow]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /><ref name="BTM" /> It was surmised that the temple's site was either holy or significant for primitive scientific purposes.<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref>

At some point, either as part of the original intent of the building or through ulterior additions, the Ordu Aspectu used the Great Temple to store data, including a map room giving directions to the [[Citadel of Rur]] on [[Garn]].<ref name="Helmet Collection">{{HelmetCollectionCite|76|Databank A-Z}}</ref>

The Massassi eventually went extinct [[Millennium|millennia]]<ref name="Doctor Aphra 3">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 3|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 3]]</ref> before [[0 ABY]],<ref name="Aphra 3 Date">{{Aphra2016Date|3}}</ref> sometime after finishing their temples.<ref name="Helmet Collection" /> Over five [[Millennium|thousand years]] after its construction,<ref name="BTM" /> the Great Temple was rediscovered by<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> the yet to be formalized<ref name="Messenger">{{Andor|Messenger}}</ref> [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]].<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> In specific, it was being used by the [[Massassi Group]] rebel cell.<ref name="Rogue One Visual Guide" /> Nonetheless, it was intended to be used as the Alliance's main base by rebel organizers [[Mon Mothma]] and [[Bail Prestor Organa]] once the rebellion was ready.<ref name="Welcome">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref> Rebel [[engineer]]s converted the large structure into its base of operations,<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> designating it Base One.<ref name="Episode IV" /> From the Massassi Base, [[Jyn Erso]], [[K-2SO]], and [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] traveled to [[Eadu]]. The Alliance then launched a force of [[X-wing starfighter|X-wings]] and [[BTL Y-wing starfighter|Y-wings]] to the planet from the base. Later, when [[Rogue One]] was trapped on [[Scarif]], nearly all of the Rebel forces at Massassi Base were sent with the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]] to [[Battle of Scarif|attack]] the planet.<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

After successfully [[Battle of Yavin|attacking]] the Empire's [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] from the Temple, the Alliance was forced to [[Evacuation of Yavin 4|evacuate]] [[Yavin 4]] for fear of retaliation.<ref name="Princess Leia 1">[[Princess Leia 1|''Princess Leia'' 1]]</ref> At some point following their departure, the Empire took over the Great Temple.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 2">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 2|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 2]]</ref>

==Layout==
[[File:Yavin_landing_pad.png|thumb|right|250px|The Great Temple's exterior featured an extensive landing pad for Rebel starfighters.]]
The Great Temple was a lofty pyramidal structure consisting of a number of successively receding stories and a high-ceilinged chamber at the top. It was built from huge blocks of [[stone]] hewed from Yavin 4's crust, with no visible signs of advanced machinery. After the Alliance to Restore the Republic took possession of the building, it arranged the Great Temple according to its needs, drilling new cavities and reinforcing the interior walls with sheets of seamed metal and the stone floors with [[ferrocrete]]. The Rebels also added elevators from the subterranean level to the open hangar.<ref name="CL 2016" />

With the Rebel additions, the base was large enough to hold at least sixty fighters and two [[Gallofree Yards, Inc.|Gallofree Yards]] [[GR-75 medium transport]]s. The base's barracks had space for thousands of soldiers.<ref name="CL 2016" /> Though this was plenty of space, there were not enough bunks for every soldier, so some fashioned hammocks from cargo nets.<ref name="Rebel Files>''[[Star Wars: The Rebel Files]]''</ref>

Deep below the surface of the moon were survival bunkers, connected to the temple with [[turbolift]]s. The Alliance installed them as a "last refuge" in the event of an Imperial planetary bombardment.<ref name="CL 2016" />

